          "filename": "Cornelius Grogan 1798 memorial at Redmondstown church - geograph.org.uk - 1274528.jpg",
          "caption": "Cornelius Grogan 1798 memorial at Redmondstown church The churchyard of Redmondstown church, Rathaspick, contains this memorial to the protestant Cornelius Grogan of Johnstown Castle, executed on Wexford bridge in 1798, whose body is in the graveyard. He was a Wexford area commander in the 1798 rebellion, and the memorial was unveiled in 1998.",
